{
  "inShort": "I checked the sprint’s links: the team finished behind, with the goal unproven. The devlog clears the prototyping requirement, but no openable build or five-player notes support the reported results. Mia stopped confirming work after week one, leaving only Alex’s work confirmed for sailing and testing.",
  "discussed": [
    {
      "itemId": "cmvtjvqa407chnxz8px563av7",
      "text": "The public repository contains Godot demos, an MIT license and import instructions. It closes the reference task, but does not show your playable slice."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvtjvqc007cinxz8malbx2fr",
      "text": "The sprint links Big Buck Bunny again. Its title and thumbnail identify an animated film; the video itself was not watched. The reference task remains done, but this does not demonstrate islands, tides or co-op sailing. The landscape photo does not demonstrate them either."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvtjvqcw07cjnxz8pdhgkj7t",
      "text": "The Wikipedia article explains playtesting and its formats, closing the reading-reference task. It supplies no results from your five-player test."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvtjvqds07cknxz8v6h3pm2y",
      "text": "The private design board remains done. Its contents were not assessed here, so it supplies no verified evidence for the playable slice."
    }
  ],
  "notDiscussed": [],
  "outsidePlan": [],
  "questions": [
    "Did the five players test two-player sailing, and what did that test reveal?",
    "Missing proof is common and can be addressed next checkpoint. Publish an openable build with both islands, tides and co-op sailing, alongside the five-player notes. At the next checkpoint, I look forward to seeing your devlogs, artifacts and project activity ;)."
  ]
}

